      "object_id": "mathia_interpretation_14479af32d823e41457faa978dcfc135f851783aaadc7f63349d551c24cd8189",
      "object_role": "interpretation",
      "proposed_content": "The introduction decomposes the first-derivative zero problem by region and proof status. Assuming the Riemann hypothesis, it claims zero exclusion in the open left half of the critical strip, 0 < Re(s) < 1/2; for the closed left half-plane it claims only a reduction to a feasible calculation. Its named intermediate aim is a modified form of the earlier conjecture, so the derivation from that target to the regional conclusions remains a proof burden outside this span. The span also announces results about increase while moving left from Re(s) = 1/2, but OCR damage prevents safe identification of the exact quantity.",
